<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="book_route.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1">
<metadata><name>Tam McArthur Rim from Dutchman Flat</name><desc>or-vielbig-2e:268-1: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.999772" lon="-121.663687"><ele>1935.4</ele><name>Dutchman Flat Sno-park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (OSM way 559496151); confidence: high; pdf_page: 267; book_elev_ft: 6400; quote: map 60: DUTCHMAN FLAT NORDIC SNO-PARK 6400'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.028440" lon="-121.665390"><ele>1974.7</ele><name>Little Meadow (Big Meadow Trail / Pete's Way)</name><desc>source: OSM junction of the nordic Big Meadow Trail (way 1467651000) and Pete's Way (way 662808005); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 268; book_elev_ft: 6450; quote: in 2.2 miles from the sno-park it enters Little Meadow ... Both Pete's Way and Swampy Lakes Trails exit from this meadow</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.034030" lon="-121.677070"><ele>2001.4</ele><name>Big Meadow west end (road 370)</name><desc>source: OSM node where Big Meadow Trail, Todd Ridge Trail and NF 370 meet; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 270; book_elev_ft: 6450; quote: then to the west end of Big Meadow and up the road to a blufftop viewpoint (PDF 270); Todd Ridge trail starts at the west end of Big Meadow (PDF 268)</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.037790" lon="-121.671790"><ele>2058.7</ele><name>Blufftop viewpoint on road 370</name><desc>source: point on OSM NF 370 0.4 mi by road before the 370/378 junction (map 60 '0.4'); georef of the map dot gives 44.0354,-121.6715, 270 m away; confidence: low; pdf_page: 267; book_elev_ft: 6700; quote: up the road to a blufftop viewpoint; map 60: 6700' star, 0.4 to 6780'</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.041652" lon="-121.667439"><ele>2069.6</ele><name>Road 370 / 378 junction (6,780 ft)</name><desc>source: OSM junction NF 370 x NF 378 (road to Crater Ditch trailhead = map's Crater Ck Ditch route); 0.84 mi by road to the 370/380 junction vs map 0.8; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 267; book_elev_ft: 6780; quote: map 60: 6780' junction, CRATER CK DITCH ROUTE TO LOWER CRATER</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.048674" lon="-121.655352"><ele>2108.2</ele><name>Road 370 / 380 junction (6,880 ft), east of Moon Mtn</name><desc>source: OSM node 38483518 (NF 370 x NF 380); USGS topo labels it 370/380 J; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 267; book_elev_ft: 6880; quote: map 60: 6880' junction where the OFF-TRAIL ROUTE TO TAM McARTHUR RIM - 3.5 MILES FROM MOON MTN begins</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.051300" lon="-121.653700"><ele>2107.5</ele><name>Leave road 370 at its bend (start of the dotted off-trail line)</name><desc>source: book map 60 dotted line 'OFF-TRAIL ROUTE TO TAM McARTHUR RIM', read from the ink overlay (notes/overlay-map60-tam-mcarthur.md); the bend is in OSM NF 370, so this does not depend on the map fit; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 267; quote: map 60: OFF-TRAIL ROUTE TO TAM McARTHUR RIM - 3.5 MILES FROM MOON MTN</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.059700" lon="-121.656800"><ele>2159.1</ele><name>Off-trail line, map 60 (about +/-300 m)</name><desc>source: book map 60 dotted line 'OFF-TRAIL ROUTE TO TAM McARTHUR RIM', read from the ink overlay (notes/overlay-map60-tam-mcarthur.md); mean of three fits; confidence: low; pdf_page: 267; quote: map 60 dotted line</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.068000" lon="-121.656500"><ele>2195.6</ele><name>Off-trail line continued past the map edge, level with Ball Butte (about +/-350 m)</name><desc>source: book map 60 dotted line 'OFF-TRAIL ROUTE TO TAM McARTHUR RIM', read from the ink overlay (notes/overlay-map60-tam-mcarthur.md); the dotted line extended to Ball Butte's latitude. Replaces the earlier guess at 44.068,-121.662, 440 m further west; confidence: low; pdf_page: 267; quote: around the east side of Ball Butte</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="44.093000" lon="-121.643700"><ele>2357.9</ele><name>Tam McArthur Rim viewpoint</name><desc>source: west end of OSM Tam McArthur Rim Trail #4078 (way 278139719) on the rim edge; GNIS cliff 1150850 is 470 m west. The book's star could not be georeferenced (map 60 is compressed at its top edge); confidence: low; pdf_page: 270; book_elev_ft: 7800; quote: climbs 1,400 feet to a high point of 7,800 feet; Just 2 miles east of the jagged summit of Broken Top</desc></wpt>
<trk><name>Tam McArthur Rim from Dutchman Flat</name><desc>1. Dutchman Flat Sno-park -&gt; Little Meadow (Big Meadow Trail / Pete's Way): osm (high), 2.57 mi | 2. Little Meadow (Big Meadow Trail / Pete's Way) -&gt; Big Meadow west end (road 370): osm (high), 0.91 mi | 3. Big Meadow west end (road 370) -&gt; Blufftop viewpoint on road 370: osm (high), 0.63 mi | 4. Blufftop viewpoint on road 370 -&gt; Road 370 / 378 junction (6,780 ft): osm (high), 0.47 mi | 5. Road 370 / 378 junction (6,780 ft) -&gt; Road 370 / 380 junction (6,880 ft), east of Moon Mtn: osm (medium), 0.84 mi | 6. Road 370 / 380 junction (6,880 ft), east of Moon Mtn -&gt; Leave road 370 at its bend (start of the dotted off-trail line): osm (medium), 0.23 mi | 7. Leave road 370 at its bend (start of the dotted off-trail line) -&gt; Off-trail line, map 60 (about +/-300 m): straight (low), 0.60 mi | 8. Off-trail line, map 60 (about +/-300 m) -&gt; Off-trail line continued past the map edge, level with Ball Butte (about +/-350 m): straight (low), 0.57 mi | 9. Off-trail line continued past the map edge, level with Ball Butte (about +/-350 m) -&gt; Tam McArthur Rim viewpoint: straight (low), 1.84 mi</desc>
